From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: optimize VP uplink TX

Declare EDMA features before registration so DSA and VLAN devices inherit
scatter-gather and segmentation capabilities. Keep QCA4B checksum restrictions
and later user feature changes intact.

Batch software GSO producer publications with a 32-descriptor bound, retaining
TX queue serialization, per-segment DMA ownership and BQL accounting. Publish
pending packets before checking an insufficient descriptor cache and at the
end of the list, including after mapping failures.

Reuse the precomputed scatter-gather descriptor count within a batch.
GSO failures retain the original skb for the software path.

Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
---
